<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ămĕthystĭnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		amethystus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of the color of amethyst</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					1, 97, 7</span></i>
			.—Also <i>absol.</i>: amethystina (sc.
			vestimenta), * <i><span class="en">Juv. 7,
			136</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Set</i> or <i>adorned with
			amethyst</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trientes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 49</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
